; exclude_spin_model: EXCLUDE on a spin {-1, +1} model raises NonBinaryModel.
;
; EXCLUDE writes a mutual-exclusion penalty on variables 0 and 1, and spec/xqvm/HLF.md derives
; every constraint expansion under x^2 = x, which holds only for binary
; variables. On any other domain the same terms encode a different penalty,
; so spec/xqvm/ISA.md has EXCLUDE raise NonBinaryModel instead. Every other
; operand is valid, so the domain check alone decides.

PUSH 4
SQMX r0          ; spin model, 4 variables
PUSH 0           ; i
PUSH 1           ; j
PUSH 5           ; penalty
EXCLUDE r0
HALT
